From: Keel maintainers <maintainers@keel.dev>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] preserve runtime environment for endpointless Linux launches

Local incremental patch record against Keel's reviewed
@anthropic-ai/sandbox-runtime v0.0.59 postimage
(upstream 3f4233f173227ca2e9dfde8c4985bc31811a64fc).

The reviewed postimage is carried in these vendored paths:

- src/sandbox/linux-sandbox-utils.ts
- test/sandbox/launch-authority-lifecycle.test.ts
- test/sandbox/launch-authority.test.ts

Root cause:

The Linux wrapper emitted generateProxyEnvVars() only inside the authenticated
HTTP/SOCKS bridge branch. A profile that structurally denied all network access
correctly received no endpoints, token, or proxy authority, but consequently
also missed the non-secret SANDBOX_RUNTIME marker and the Warden-selected
TMPDIR. The temp root remained mounted and writable, yet ordinary child temp
file APIs could not discover it.

Contract anchors required by Keel's vendor verifier:

- endpointless profiles receive SANDBOX_RUNTIME=1
- endpointless filesystem profiles receive the trusted sandbox-owned TMPDIR
- proxy credentials and CA paths require both authenticated bridge sockets
- empty bridge paths cannot project proxy credentials or CA paths
- endpointless profiles retain no HTTP, HTTPS, SOCKS, token, or host-port state
- filesystem, network, credential, TLS, audit, policy, and retry authority are
  unchanged

Evidence:

- a real Linux bubblewrap launch asserts the exact child TMPDIR key rather than
  matching the CLAUDE_CODE_TMPDIR substring;
- the same launch asserts SANDBOX_RUNTIME and rejects every proxy environment
  spelling while retaining the existing no-endpoint checks;
- an emitted-argv regression passes empty bridge paths alongside credential and
  CA canaries and proves none of that proxy authority reaches the child;
- the spawned-Warden filesystem probe runs node --test, writes through TMPDIR,
  verifies the owner-only root, and retains all neighboring denial probes.

Security and compatibility:

The patch moves runtime environment emission outside the proxy-socket branch.
It still passes proxy ports, proxy authentication, and CA trust paths to
generateProxyEnvVars() only when both authenticated bridge sockets exist.
Profiles without filesystem restrictions preserve the inherited TMPDIR exactly
as before. The patch is minimal and upstreamable; recorded 2026-08-13 and not
yet submitted upstream.
